<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45939" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sublātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f. [tollo), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a lifting up</i>, <i>raising</i>, <i>elevation.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: a sublatione (soni) ad positionem, <i>an upward beat</i> in marking time, <i><span class="en">Quint. 9,
				4, 48</span></i>; so (opp. positio) <i><span class="en">id. 9, 4, 48, §
			55</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b> * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> In gen., <i>an elevation</i>, <i>exaltation</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fin. 2, 4, 13</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In
			partic., <i>a removal</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">furtiva,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ambros. in Luc. 5, § 112</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>An abrogation</i>, <i>annulling</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">judicii,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 7, 1, 60</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
